{number: 60}
{title: Break Thou the Bread of Life}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Break thou the bread of life, [F] dear Lord, to [C] me,
As thou didst [Am] break the [F] loaves be-[C] side the [G7] sea;
[C] Beyond the sacred page I [F] seek thee, [C] Lord,
My spirit [Am] pants for [F] thee, O [C] living [G7] [C] Word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Bless thou the truth, dear Lord, to [F] me, to [C] me,
As thou didst [Am] bless the [F] bread by [C] Gali-[G7] lee;
[C] Then shall all bondage cease, all [F] fetters [C] fall;
And I shall [Am] find my [F] peace, my [C] All in [G7] [C] all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Thou art the Bread of Life, O [F] Lord, to [C] me,
Thy holy [Am] Word the [F] truth that [C] saveth [G7] me;
[C] Give me to eat and live with [F] thee a-[C] bove;
Teach me to [Am] love thy [F] truth, for [C] thou art [G7] [C] love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [C] send thy Spirit, Lord, now [F] unto [C] me,
That he may [Am] touch mine [F] eyes, and [C] make me [G7] see:
[C] Show me the truth concealed with-[F] in thy [C] Word,
And in thy [Am] Book re-[F] vealed I [C] see the [G7] [C] Lord.
{end_of_verse}
